From 6c5409caa828847c1c745eff9d319c9613ec1959 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lawsir <lawsir@mac-mini-hermes>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:32:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] chore(build): stop tracking the 21 hipify-generated
 .hip files

These are build artefacts, not sources. Proven, not assumed:

  - The driver is PyTorch's builtin hipify (torch/utils/cpp_extension.py:1482-1498),
    not a script in this repo - which is why grepping the repo found nothing.
  - hipify_python.py:978-1001 writes the output only when it is missing OR its
    content differs; otherwise it reports "[skipped, already hipified]".
  - Empirical test (2026-09-13): deleted csrc/gemm/gptq/q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.hip,
    rebuilt. The log showed "q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.cu -> q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.hip [ok]"
    (regenerated) and hipcc compiled it. The regenerated .hip hash was
    487b0f6f53fdf7b2 and the resulting common_ops .so hash was 04f4a981ca40fb68
    - both bit-identical to before the deletion.

One exception is kept tracked: csrc/allreduce/deterministic_all_reduce.hip has no
.cu sibling and is a hand-written source, so .gitignore negates it explicitly.

The 22 files remain on disk; only the index changed. This removes 46% of the
local diff volume, which was previously pure .cu/.hip mirror noise.
